---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import StatusGovernance from "../components/StatusGovernance.astro";
import ProjectUpdates from "../components/ProjectUpdates.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Circular Justice" description="An individual research and evidence-building initiative exploring whether safe surplus-food redistribution could support affordable meals through the Unity House community model.">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Individual research initiative · evidence-building</p>
    <h1>Circular Justice</h1>
    <p class="lead">Circular Justice is an individual research initiative exploring whether a coordinated local surplus-food model could reduce avoidable waste and improve access to affordable meals through the Unity House community-centre model. The work is at the research and feasibility stage; an operational pilot has not been approved.</p>
  </section>

  <StatusGovernance stage="Research / evidence-building" operator="Individual research initiative; a future delivery operator has not been selected." delivery="Desk research and feasibility development. No Circular Justice collection, app or food service is operating." partnership="No supermarket, redistribution-operator, council or government partnership is established for Circular Justice." funding="No Circular Justice pilot funding or approval is confirmed." boundary="The separate Unity House award funds six hosted community health and wellbeing sessions in South Waltham Forest during September 2026–March 2027. It does not fund or approve a Circular Justice surplus-food operation, permanent centre or UK-wide service." facts={[{label:"Pilot status",value:"Not yet approved; no collection or meal operation is claimed."},{label:"VNM logistics assets",value:"No owned vans, donor app or food-handling network are claimed."}]} />

  <section class="section question">
    <p class="eyebrow">The question we are testing</p>
    <h2>Can local surplus become safe, affordable community food?</h2>
    <p>Could suitable surplus from households, shops, supermarkets and other food businesses be coordinated with existing redistribution and logistics partners, then used through a trusted Unity House host for redistribution, shared learning and low-cost meals? Research must establish the need, safe supply, responsible operating model, cost and partner capacity before a bounded pilot is proposed.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section pathways">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why food surplus first</p>
      <h2>Follow food to its safest useful route</h2>
      <p>Food is the first research pathway because the Unity House pilot already includes healthy meal preparation, low-cost nutrition and food-waste learning. That is a relevant starting point for feasibility work, not evidence that a surplus supply or service is ready.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cards">
      <article class="card vnm-glass-card"><h3>Suitable edible surplus</h3><p>Research whether food that remains safe, traceable and legally suitable can be redistributed or used in meals under clear donor, storage, transport, preparation and allergen controls.</p></article>
      <article class="card vnm-glass-card"><h3>Other reusable items</h3><p>Residents may be able to offer suitable reusable items in a future service, subject to separate acceptance criteria, safeguarding, liability and handling arrangements. Food and non-food routes would need distinct rules.</p></article>
      <article class="card vnm-glass-card"><h3>Unavoidable food waste</h3><p>Material that is not suitable for people to eat must not be presented as food. Any separate treatment route would need an authorised, competent operator and applicable waste controls.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section pilot">
    <p class="eyebrow">Proposed bounded pilot · subject to evidence and approval</p>
    <h2>Coordinate existing capability around a local host</h2>
    <p>A future pilot could test a local coordination layer that links donors with existing operators. It would explore partners that already have suitable apps, vans, food-handling systems and logistics capacity; VNM does not currently claim to own these assets. The exact operator, host, locality, food stream and service design remain to be identified.</p>
    <ol class="flow" aria-label="Possible future pilot flow">
      <li><strong>1</strong><span>Resident or business offers eligible surplus</span></li>
      <li><strong>2</strong><span>Partner intake checks suitability and availability</span></li>
      <li><strong>3</strong><span>Existing collection and logistics operator coordinates safe handling</span></li>
      <li><strong>4</strong><span>Unity House host receives an agreed, traceable supply</span></li>
      <li><strong>5</strong><span>Suitable food is redistributed or prepared as affordable meals</span></li>
    </ol>
    <p class="note"><strong>Illustrative pathway only.</strong> It describes a model to investigate, not current service, partner commitments or approved pilot activity.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section measure">
    <div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">Evidence before claims</p><h2>What a pilot would need to measure</h2><p>Measures and collection methods should be agreed with the host, delivery partners and residents, using proportionate and privacy-conscious evaluation.</p></div>
    <div class="measure-grid">
      <span>Eligible surplus received and diverted from disposal</span><span>Food safety, traceability and compliance</span><span>Meal cost, affordability and resident access</span><span>Resident and business participation</span><span>Collection cost and partner workload</span><span>Volunteer, training and paid-job opportunities</span><span>Resident experience and community outcomes</span><span>Reliability, unused supply and operating limits</span>
    </div>
    <p class="note">These are proposed measures, not achieved results or promised benefits. Any employment or training pathway depends on a viable, funded operating model.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section partners">
    <p class="eyebrow">What partners and public bodies could enable</p>
    <h2>Resolve responsibilities before collection begins</h2>
    <p>Councils, government, food businesses, community hosts and experienced redistribution operators could help determine whether a safe, lawful and affordable model is feasible. Relevant public-sector involvement may include permissions, premises, procurement or funding routes, food-safety and public-health coordination, waste and food-classification advice, evaluation and any later scaling decision. No such support is confirmed for Circular Justice.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Agree who is responsible for donors, collection, transport, storage, preparation, redistribution and records.</li>
      <li>Confirm food hygiene, temperature control, date marking, traceability, allergen information and recall procedures.</li>
      <li>Check food and waste classification, environmental and local-authority requirements, premises, insurance and procurement.</li>
      <li>Set proportionate privacy, safeguarding, volunteer, training and incident-reporting arrangements.</li>
      <li>Secure a viable budget, partner capacity, evaluation plan and resident consent before any pilot launch.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section pathway">
    <p class="eyebrow">Evidence → pilot → evaluation → replication</p>
    <h2>One local test at a time</h2>
    <div class="stages"><article><strong>01 · Research</strong><p>Map local need, existing services, food streams, rules, potential hosts and operators.</p></article><article><strong>02 · Design</strong><p>Co-design a bounded pilot with residents and partners, with named responsibilities and approvals.</p></article><article><strong>03 · Evaluate</strong><p>Measure safety, access, costs, partner workload, participation and outcomes against agreed criteria.</p></article><article><strong>04 · Decide</strong><p>Continue, adapt or stop based on findings. Consider another locality only if evidence, funding and permissions support it.</p></article></div>
    <p class="status-note"><strong>Current status: Research / evidence-building. Pilot not yet approved.</strong> Circular Justice is not proven, funded, government-backed or operating nationwide. Any UK-scale model is a later hypothesis that would require positive evaluation and separate decisions.</p>
  </section>

  <p class="contact"><a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Discuss research or partnership fit</a><a class="text-link" href="/unity-house">Read about the Unity House pilot →</a></p>
  <ProjectUpdates project="circular-justice" />

  <style>
    .hero{max-width:90ch;padding:8px 0 18px}.eyebrow{margin:0 0 9px;color:#0f766e;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;font-size:12px;font-weight:850}h1{margin:0 0 12px;font-size:clamp(42px,6vw,64px);letter-spacing:-.04em;color:var(--text)}h2{margin:0 0 10px;color:var(--text);font-size:clamp(24px,3.6vw,34px);letter-spacing:-.025em}.lead,.section>p:not(.eyebrow),.section-head>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:90ch;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;font-size:17px}.lead{font-size:19px}.section{margin-top:34px}.question,.pilot,.partners,.pathway{padding:clamp(19px,3vw,28px);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:20px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.06),rgba(16,185,129,.07))}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:13px;margin-top:15px}.card{padding:17px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:17px;background:var(--glass)}.card h3{margin:0 0 8px;color:var(--text);font-size:17px}.card p{margin:0;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7}.flow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,minmax(0,1fr));gap:10px;padding:0;margin:20px 0 0;list-style:none}.flow li{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:9px;padding:13px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.68);color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55;font-size:14px}.flow strong{display:grid;place-items:center;flex:0 0 27px;height:27px;border-radius:50%;background:rgba(39,99,235,.12);color:#1d4ed8}.note{margin:15px 0 0;padding:12px 14px;border-left:3px solid #d97706;background:rgba(245,158,11,.09);color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65;font-size:14px}.measure-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:10px;margin-top:16px}.measure-grid span,.stages article{padding:14px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.72);color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6}.partners ul{padding-left:22px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75}.partners li+li{margin-top:6px}.stages{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:11px;margin-top:16px}.stages strong{color:#0f766e}.stages p{margin:7px 0 0;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65;font-size:14px}.status-note{margin:17px 0 0;padding:14px;border:1px solid rgba(15,118,110,.22);border-radius:14px;background:rgba(16,185,129,.07);color:var(--text);line-height:1.7}.contact{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:22px}.btn{display:inline-flex;padding:11px 15px;border:1px solid rgba(37,99,235,.25);border-radius:14px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(39,99,235,.10),rgba(16,185,129,.10));color:var(--text);text-decoration:none;font-weight:850}.text-link{color:#1d4ed8;font-weight:750}@media(max-width:950px){.flow{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}.measure-grid,.stages{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:650px){.cards,.flow,.measure-grid,.stages{grid-template-columns:1fr}.contact{align-items:stretch}.btn{text-align:center;justify-content:center}}
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
